.TH PACK 1 "August 2026" "pack-extract 1.5.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pack \- create compressed archives in the specified format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pack
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.br
.B pack
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B pack
.I format source
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pack
creates an archive or compressed file from the given
.I source
(file or directory) in the specified
.IR format
using
.BR libarchive (3).
The output is placed in the current directory, named
.IB source . format
(for example
.BR report.txt.gz ).
.PP
This avoids having to remember tool-specific flags for each format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.SS Archive formats (files and directories)
.TS
l l l.
Format	Extension	Backend
_
tar	.tar	libarchive
tar.gz	.tar.gz	libarchive
tar.xz	.tar.xz	libarchive
tar.bz2	.tar.bz2	libarchive
tar.zst	.tar.zst	libarchive
tar.lz4	.tar.lz4	libarchive
tar.lz	.tar.lz	libarchive
tar.lzo	.tar.lzo	libarchive
tar.br	.tar.br	libarchive (optional)
zip	.zip	libarchive
7z	.7z	libarchive
.TE
.SS Single-file compression (files only)
.TS
l l l.
Format	Extension	Backend
_
gz	.gz	libarchive
bz2	.bz2	libarchive
xz	.xz	libarchive
zstd	.zstd	libarchive
lz4	.lz4	libarchive
lzo	.lzo	libarchive
br	.br	libarchive (optional)
.TE
.PP
Single-file formats refuse directories; use an archive format instead.
.B tar.br
and
.B br
are compiled only when
.B ARCHIVE_FILTER_BROTLI
is available in the installed libarchive headers.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a gzip-compressed tarball of a directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack tar.gz project/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a zip archive:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack zip src/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compress a single file with gzip:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ pack gz report.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Archive created successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (source not found, unsupported format, directory with
single-file format, creation failure).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B pack
links against
.BR libarchive (3).
Build requires the libarchive development package and
.BR pkg-config (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR extract (1),
.BR libarchive (3)
